.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PCI_HOTPLUG 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pci_hotplug_poll ,
.Nm pci_hotplug_add ,
.Nm pci_hotplug_remove
.Nd poll and reconcile PCI device hotplug state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/pci.h
.Ft void
.Fn pci_hotplug_poll void
.Ft int
.Fn pci_hotplug_add "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot"
.Ft int
.Fn pci_hotplug_remove "pci_device_t *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions reconcile the PCI device list with current configuration
space visibility and create or remove driver-model devices accordingly.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The add and remove functions return 0 or a positive device count on
success, and a negative error code on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pci_scan 9
